# Known secret shapes, one POSIX extended regular expression per line.
#
# The one list of what shirabe treats as a secret: the public-content check
# (scripts/ablation/check-public-content.sh) refuses a line matching any of
# them, and `shirabe question raise` refuses question content matching any of
# them, reading this file built into the binary. Lines starting with `#` and
# blank lines are ignored. Each pattern must mean the same under grep -E and
# Rust's regex crate: character classes, counted repetition and literals only.
gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{20,}
github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{20,}
sk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}
AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}
xox[abprs]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}
-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----
